id: pm-ljrh29
title: "Outcome milestone: multi-decade continuity — readable, migratable, privacy-governed proof across generations of formats and cryptography"
description: Prove that a pm workspace remains understandable verifiable restorable and governable across decades of schema format cryptographic organizational and legal change. This milestone composes existing history attestation compatibility format migration retention and lawful-erasure work into a long-lived institutional-memory outcome.
type: Milestone
status: open
priority: 3
tags[9]: "area:history","area:privacy",continuity,"horizon:far",immutability,milestone,outcome,roadmap,standards
created_at: "2026-08-14T14:35:39.995Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-28T07:21:58.093Z"
deadline: "2036-12-31T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 129600
acceptance_criteria: "A multi-decade synthetic corpus spanning every supported format and schema generation is readable queryable and independently verifiable by the public SDK; Every format cryptographic and schema migration is lossless resumable idempotent and represented by new immutable evidence rather than silent rewrite; Retention lawful erasure archival and proof-preserving redaction policies have executable conformance tests and explicit jurisdiction-neutral extension points; Cryptographic algorithm agility is declared in the proof format and at least one full algorithm migration is proven without invalidating prior attestations; Restoration at sampled versions across the complete supported window reproduces item workspace and relationship state byte-equivalently where the contract promises byte identity; Documentation separates append-only API behavior, hash-chain tamper evidence, authenticated authorship and externally anchored proof guarantees"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Preserve trustworthy institutional context across generations of software organizations and policy
value: The tracker remains a durable source of truth rather than becoming an unreadable archive after format or cryptographic change
impact: Connects immutable history portability compatibility migration retention and privacy into one evidence-gated continuity contract
outcome: A publicly specified and independently testable multi-decade continuity guarantee
why_now: Provable history ends at restoration under current contracts while already-tracked compatibility erasure and cryptographic agility work has no later portfolio outcome
parent: pm-doxj
risk: critical
confidence: low
expected_result: "A synthetic multi-decade corpus spanning every format and schema generation remains readable, queryable and independently verifiable, with every migration lossless and represented as new evidence."
