notes[3]:
  - created_at: "2026-08-24T14:27:59.779Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Continuity programme organization 2026-08-24: durability is evaluated across independent axes rather than as one distant date. Format continuity is owned by the open workspace specification and conformance suite; state continuity by item and workspace point-in-time reconstruction; proof continuity by algorithm-agile chains and portable detached attestations; semantic continuity by versioned relationship and operation vocabularies; organizational continuity by federation, signatures, and policy migration; legal continuity by retention and proof-preserving erasure; consumer continuity by re-derivable token and latency budgets. Added explicit verifies edges from pm-4jk8kx, pm-3z0k, and pm-5gf0xf to this outcome; pm-pae3wo already verifies it. Promotion requires a synthetic corpus spanning multiple format, schema, policy, organization, and cryptographic generations plus independent-reader proof. No additional calendar milestone is needed because this item already owns the multi-decade outcome."
  - created_at: "2026-09-08T06:02:18.223Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Decade-scale continuity design: publish independently implementable format semantics and conformance vectors; retain explicit format/cryptographic algorithm identifiers; verify old supported readers against new writers and old history against current replay. Detached proof bundles need trusted externally retained checkpoints or signatures to resist complete-chain replacement; a local hash chain alone establishes internal tamper evidence. Plan key rotation, crypto-agility, offline verification, data minimization and legal redaction with visible proof boundaries. Annual compatibility drills should restore a real historical fixture without this checkout or its caches. No retention promise depends on one vendor, one model tokenizer or an unversioned extension."
  - created_at: "2026-09-28T05:51:45.472Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Continuity design 2026-09-28: maintain a versioned reader/migrator matrix and archival manifests with content hashes, schema versions and algorithm identifiers. Test 30-year synthetic histories through old-to-new and interrupted migrations, item deletion/restoration, key rotation and proof-preserving redaction. Hash chains establish tamper evidence relative to a trusted anchor, not physical impossibility of editing bytes. Independent witnesses or signed checkpoints and key revocation policy are required before stronger immutable-proof claims. Sample restores at every format boundary and both sides of branch merges, with metadata and graph state included."
    edited_at: "2026-09-28T07:21:57.161Z"
